<title>USA: Cade Industries wins $17.1 mln in orders.</title>
<headline>Cade Industries wins $17.1 mln in orders.</headline>
<dateline>LANSING, Mich. 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cade Industries Inc said Wednesday it received $17.1 million in new contracts during the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>With the addition of these new orders, Cade's backlog increased to $40.2 million as of March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>The contracts, scheduled for delivery over the next two years, were received from several of the leading aerospace manufacturers, including Textron Inc's Bell Helicopter, United Technologies Corp's Pratt &amp; Whitney, Northrop Grumman Corp, Boeing Co, Rolls-Royce Plc, General Electric Co, and CFMI.</p>
<p>The contracts were for the manufacture of components within Cade's three core product areas: gas turbine engine products, airframe products and jet engine test equipment.</p>
